  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a hybrid fraud‑detection framework (TransGuard‑QNet) combining iXGBoost, QNN, QAE, k‑means, and LP-based weight optimization. On a Kaggle Financial Risk dataset with an 80:20 split, the system reports 99.095% accuracy, 99.512% precision, and 98.591% F1 score, outperforming baseline models such as XGBoost (~96.8% accuracy) and k‑means (~95.1%). All experiments were implemented in Python on a classical CPU with no reported quantum hardware execution.",
